      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a7ac88bf5a5c52c08064fb9|full_name}: not true. If the program managing the avatar database was to run a quick performance check on the avatar after it has been uploaded it can add a preference tag to the avatar so when it comes time for the client to load all the players the client can skip the download of any tags that are not in the range of the users safety settings. The database all ready runs a check for avatar names even if they are uploaded as private and will rename any avatar who's name is on the list. Like the last time I tried to upload a avatar with the word Trump in the name i.e. \"Trump card\" it renamed the Trump part of the avatar name to something stupid.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
