      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b3406530132a20f8f95c128|full_name}: Having something check for a blacklisted variable vs having servers checking each avatar uploaded, every time, is not the same.\n\nThe cost in checking for variables is so small you won't even see it.\n\nBut checking for avatars, they first need to download the avatar from the CDN, unpack it, run it thought the script, get and calculate the info, submit it to the DB, then remove everything and start over.\nThis is very costly and requires multiple instances to be run at the same time for it to be efficient with the current rate people upload and update their avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
