  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-09-05T16:17:00.128Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed when I'm in public worlds with my safety settings on, all avatars will be downloaded and ones that go higher than the performance options you have set will only be hidden after they have finished loading. This tells me that despite having them hidden, they still get cached and fully downloaded. I think a way to make things easier on the vrc clients would be to determine whether or not to hide an avatar *before* it gets downloaded, probably with server side enforcement rather than just client side. This would probably help with memory leak issues a little bit. So basically, the server would keep track of the performance ranks and would tell the client if it's okay to download or not based on the client's settings.",
